{% comment %}
  od-fonts
  The typefaces the Figma specifies, self-hosted.

  Rendered by the sections that need them, so a page without those sections
  never downloads the files.

  Why self-hosted rather than substituted:
  the design's faces are La Belle Aurore, Pinyon Script, Instrument Serif, Inter,
  Helvetica and Roboto. All four of the first group are Google Fonts released
  under the SIL Open Font License, which permits web use — so the brief's
  "substitute the closest reasonable alternative" case doesn't arise for them.
  Inter and Roboto are in Shopify's own font library and Helvetica is a system
  face, so those three are picked up from the stacks in od-base.css and need no
  download.

  Why self-hosted rather than linked from Google:
  a <link> to fonts.googleapis.com is a third-party request on every page load,
  an extra DNS lookup and connection before any text can paint. Serving from the
  theme's own assets keeps it on one connection Shopify already has open.

  Files this expects in assets/ (woff2 only — every browser that matters has
  supported it for years, and woff2 is ~30% smaller than woff):

    LaBelleAurore-Regular.woff2
    PinyonScript-Regular.woff2
    InstrumentSerif-Regular.woff2
    InstrumentSerif-Italic.woff2

  If a file is absent the @font-face simply fails and the stack in od-base.css
  falls through to a system face — the text never disappears.

  Usage:
    {% render 'od-fonts' %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- capture od_font_faces -%}
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'La Belle Aurore';
    src: url({{ 'LaBelleAurore-Regular.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    /* swap: show the fallback immediately rather than holding the headline
       invisible while the script face downloads. */
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Pinyon Script';
    src: url({{ 'PinyonScript-Regular.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Instrument Serif';
    src: url({{ 'InstrumentSerif-Regular.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  @font-face {
    font-family: 'Instrument Serif';
    src: url({{ 'InstrumentSerif-Italic.woff2' | asset_url }}) format('woff2');
    font-weight: 400;
    font-style: italic;
    font-display: swap;
  }
{%- endcapture -%}

<style>{{ od_font_faces | strip_newlines }}</style>
